{"created": "2026-08-20T06:56:05.642413+00:00", "modified": "2026-08-20T06:56:06.024802+00:00", "id": 22019684, "conceptrecid": "22019683", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22019684", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22019683", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22019684", "metadata": {"title": "IoT-Enriched OCEL Dataset for the Cargo Pickup Process at a Major Chinese Port", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22019684", "publication_date": "2026-08-20", "description": "<p>This dataset provides an IoT-enriched Object-Centric Event Log (OCEL) capturing the cargo pickup process at a major Chinese port. It records process execution and the interactions among multiple business objects involved in the process while enriching process data with observations collected from IoT devices deployed in the operational environment.</p>\n<p>The dataset captures a practical form of IoT deployment in existing industries. Rather than fully automating the underlying business process, IoT technologies are integrated into the existing operational setting to augment process execution with real-time data. In this setting, business activities continue to be carried out according to the established process, while IoT devices provide additional observations about the operational environment and the states or movements of relevant objects to support real-time monitoring and&nbsp;decision-making.</p>\n<p>Importantly, the dataset captures both synchronous and asynchronous interactions between the business process and IoT devices. Synchronous interactions occur when sensor observations are only triggered upon the execution of process activities, whereas asynchronous interactions take place when IoT devices continuously generate observations independent of the process execution. By capturing these interactions together with object-centric process data, the dataset can be used for analysing IoT-enhanced cargo pickup processes.</p>\n<p>The dataset is designed to support research on object-centric process mining, IoT-enhanced process analysis, and logistics process analysis.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Wei, Jia", "affiliation": "Queensland University of Technology", "orcid": "0009-0002-7187-7750"}, {"name": "Song, RongJia", "affiliation": "Hangzhou Dianzi University"}, {"name": "Ouyang, Chun", "affiliation": "Queensland University of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0001-7098-5480"}, {"name": "Cui, Weiping", "affiliation": "Zhejiang University of Science and Technology"}], "keywords": ["Process Mining", "Smart Port", "Object-centric Event Log", "IoT-enriched OCEL log", "Internet of Things data"], "dates": [{"type": "available"}], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22019683"}}]}}, "title": "IoT-Enriched OCEL Dataset for the Cargo Pickup Process at a Major Chinese Port", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22019684", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22019684", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22019684?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22019684", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22019684", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22019684", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22019684/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22019683", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22019683", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22019683", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22019683", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22019684/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22019684/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22019684/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22019684/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22019684/versions/latest", "latest_html": "http